<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells 60,000/T Jun fuel oil at about $101/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells 60,000/T Jun fuel oil at about $101/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has sold by tender two 30,000-tonne cargoes of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil at around $101 per tonne for June lifting, a company source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The first cargo would be lifted in the first half of June and the other in the second half, both from Kaohsiung on a free-on-board (fob) basis, the source said.</p>
<p>In its last fuel oil sell tender, CPC sold 30,000 tonnes of high sulphur fuel oil at below $100 per tonne for lifting May 27-31 on a fob basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703571)</p>
</text>
